From e74bea6d8f71ff7048be072b6e34d59bebdea9fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rams95 <rams95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:32:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0019-bars-rain-under-hud-sharpen-map-select.patch

Cutscene black bars can be left out (the 3D under them is whole; the subtitles keep a light shade): Settings > Picture,
keys.ini black_bars. The rain on the lens stays under the game's HUD, texts and bars: the GS notes the boxes of the 2D
drawn after the game's full-screen passes (or at the front of the depth range) and the blit skips the drops there.
Contrast-adaptive sharpening of the picture (off/low/medium/high, medium by default). F6 held fast-forwards, F7 opens the
developers' map select left on the disc (PS2_DEBUG_SCENES), the card check at start answers itself (PS2_AUTO_CROSS).
F1-F9 are the program's keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QNLFPekqhcU2dj7B3Utmea
